Notes / things I was unsure about
1. Behaviour preservation: kernel edits only add emit(...) calls and read-only local assignments (correlation_id/agent_id/call_type). No signatures, return values, ordering, or locking changed; the integration test asserts traced and unconfigured runs produce identical responses.
2. syscall.started placement: emitted in _execute before syscall.start() (not inside run()) so the started→handler_invoked order is guaranteed by thread-creation happens-before, making the full 7-event sequence deterministic per correlation id.
3. Checker count semantics: resolving from P import N → P.N means multi-alias imports count once per alias; the table header was updated from "import statements" to "import names" to stay honest.
4. Demo script needed a sys.path bootstrap (sys.path.insert(0, repo_root)) because python scripts/demo_trace.py doesn't inherit pytest's pythonpath=["."].
5. Render functions in __init__.py are lazily imported (PEP 562) — still in __all__ and importable as from aios.monitoring import render_timeline, but avoids the runpy "already in sys.modules" warning for the CLI.
6. The report-only forbid_unless:* kernel rule is currently vacuous (only aios.kernel imports itself) but is proven to fire by a synthetic test; --strict ignores it.
